sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2024-collective-01> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Extending William James' definition of intelligence (reaching the same goal by different means) to collectives via the perceptual field, the region of space and time an agent can survey for alternative paths to a goal, the authors propose that as a collective grows its perceptual field increases, improving its ability to find variant paths.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A collective's perceptual field and ability to find alternative paths grow with its size";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "McMillen P, Levin M, “Collective intelligence: A unifying concept for integrating biology across scales and substrates”, Communications biology (2024), doi:10.1038/s42003-024-06037-4; section “Introduction”. Scope: Cell collectives and other biological collectives"
}
